WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.917
MICHAELA KERRISSEY: Every
day in organizations

00:00:01.917 --> 00:00:05.760
all around the globe, impromptu
teams are formed that must flexibly

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.360
collaborate regardless of
shift changes, emergency

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.560
situations, siloed specialties,
or cross-sector partnerships.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.340
AMY C. EDMONDSON: We call this
dynamic form of collaboration teaming.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.600
Teaming is a requirement
for delivering optimal care.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.847
Yet, it doesn't
necessarily come naturally.

00:00:23.847 --> 00:00:27.180
MICHAELA KERRISSEY: Professionals in the
health care and life science industries

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.120
know that their work is a team sport.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.240
What they may not know is
that the science of teaming

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.183
can help them thrive.

00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:38.100
DONALD M. BERWICK: I discovered that
outside health care had developed

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.400
a whole bunch of sciences that
supported continual improvement

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.460
and breakthroughs that health
care just had never learned.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.030
MAYA RUPERT: Being a leader does not
mean being a subject matter expert.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:50.640
Your job is to see the whole board.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.538
Everybody else gets to go
deep, and you need to go broad.

00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:56.580
MICHAELA KERRISSEY: By learning from
experts in health care and business,

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.640
you will understand how
you and your colleagues

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:06.240
can create and implement a process
of teaming within your organization.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.900
TOMISLAV MIHALJEVIC: Teamwork is not
some kind of a corporate catchphrase.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.938
Teamwork in what we do translates
into improvement of human lives.

00:01:13.938 --> 00:01:15.730
AMY C. EDMONDSON: By
the end of the course,

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:20.580
you'll appreciate what enables effective
teamwork and why teamwork can fail.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.790
You'll be able to articulate the
importance of psychological safety

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.210
and a joint problem solving
orientation and rethink

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:31.032
the role of a leader and the
organization in the context of teaming.

00:01:31.032 --> 00:01:33.240
MICHAELA KERRISSEY: Don't
leave teaming up to chance.

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.480
Draw on the science.

